"source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260719004841019754_73888a5d", "type": "Claim", "text": "In
some scholarly interpretations, the Ring of Nestor is characterized as a keimēlio (heirloom), implying that it 
functioned as an ancestral object reflecting Mycenaean practices of ancestor veneration and cultural identity.", 
